# Copy this file to `.env` in this same folder, then paste in ONE key.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The app picks whichever key it finds — you do not need to tell it which
# provider to use. With no key at all, every screen still works and
# worksheets show clearly-labelled sample content.
#
# This file is for the SEO Worksheet Studio only. Never paste a key that
# belongs to the BLC Worksheets project here, and never copy this file
# there — separate projects, separate credentials.

# ── Question writing — pick ONE ────────────────────────────────────

# Groq — fastest and has a free tier. https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# Anthropic — https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# OpenAI — https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# WHICH ONE WINS when more than one key is filled in.
# "auto" picks the first key it finds, in this order:
#       GROQ  ->  ANTHROPIC  ->  OPENAI
# So if you paste an OpenAI key in while a Groq key is still above it,
# Groq keeps being used and nothing appears to change. Either blank the
# key you have finished with, or name the one you want here:
#       LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# Valid values: auto | groq | anthropic | openai
LLM_PROVIDER=auto


# ── Pictures ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Worksheet diagrams (number lines, arrays, ten-frames, bar models,
# counters) are DRAWN BY PYTHON from a structured spec. They need no key,
# cost nothing, and are always arithmetically correct. That is the
# default and it is the right choice for maths.
#
# An image model is only worth adding for decorative or photo-real
# artwork ("children playing in a park"). Setting OPENAI_API_KEY above
# also enables that path — no separate key is needed.
#
# gpt-image-1 needs a VERIFIED OpenAI organisation. If you get a 403
# mentioning verification, change this to: dall-e-3
OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1

# ── Canva (optional, not required) ─────────────────────────────────
# Canva's Connect API arranges images you already own into a template you
# designed yourself — it does not draw original artwork from a prompt.
# https://www.canva.com/developers/
#
# STATUS: the slots below are read and `canva_configured()` reports true
# once all three are filled, but the actual Autofill call in
# app/providers/canva.py::_canva_asset is still a stub that returns None.
# It was left unimplemented on purpose — an untested integration against
# an API we cannot exercise would look finished and fail the first time
# you added real keys. Fill these in and that one function is what needs
# writing. Everything around it (when to call it, what to do when it
# fails) already works.
#
# Nothing depends on Canva: with these blank, a picture that fails
# validation is simply redrawn, and a worksheet keeps its questions.
CANVA_CLIENT_ID=
CANVA_CLIENT_SECRET=
CANVA_BRAND_TEMPLATE_ID=
